KG42.register("rules-4f3bb2a8c39678be4e276d82",{"id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R006","paper":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The SESP market subsystem manages local flexibility transactions, including settlement, billing and accounting applications. Scope: Settlement administration within the SESP market subsystem for local flexibility transactions. Flexibility revenues are paid according to the flexibility contracts under the pay-as-contract arrangement. Scope: Flexibility-provider revenues in the SESP-operated local flexibility market. Participants with activated resources are subsequently rewarded according to their flexibility contracts. Scope: Rewards to participants whose resources are activated in response to DSO requirements. Condition: The participant's resources have been activated. The flexibility cost used to determine compensation for curtailable and shiftable loads does not depend on the amount of activated energy. Scope: Compensation for flexibility supplied by curtailable and shiftable loads. Condition: Flexibility from a curtailable or shiftable load is activated. The disconnection cost equals the number of disconnected periods multiplied by the load's disconnection fee. Scope: Contractual flexibility charges for curtailable disconnectable loads. Condition: A curtailable disconnectable load is disconnected. The shifting cost equals the consumption delay multiplied by the cost per time unit established in the load's flexibility contract. Scope: Contractual flexibility charges for shiftable profile loads. Condition: A shiftable load's consumption is delayed relative to its baseline start. Generator-curtailment fees are established in the agreed flexibility contract, with prices specified period by period for reducing or disconnecting generation. Scope: Contractual flexibility charges for reducible and disconnectable generators. Condition: Generation is reduced or disconnected.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-015"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Compensation for flexibility supplied by curtailable and shiftable loads. | Contractual flexibility charges for curtailable disconnectable loads. | Contractual flexibility charges for reducible and disconnectable generators. | Contractual flexibility charges for shiftable profile loads. | Flexibility-provider revenues in the SESP-operated local flexibility market. | Rewards to participants whose resources are activated in response to DSO requirements. | Settlement administration within the SESP market subsystem for local flexibility transactions.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-008","v141-b-g01-ev-010","v141-b-g01-ev-015","v141-b-g02-ev03","v141-b-g02-ev12","v141-b-g02-ev24","v141-b-g02-ev32"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-x001","symbol":"\\delta_{k,t}^{start}","meaning":"Binary variable equal to 1 if curtailment of the disconnectable load unit k starts during period t, else 0.","kind":"operational","domain":"\\{0,1\\}","unit":null,"indices":["k \\in K^{CD}","t \\in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev18","v141-b-g04-e06"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-x002","symbol":"\\delta_{k,t}^{run}","meaning":"Binary variable equal to 1 if curtailment of the disconnectable load unit k is running during period t, else 0.","kind":"operational","domain":"\\{0,1\\}","unit":null,"indices":["k \\in K^{CD}","t \\in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev18","v141-b-g04-e06"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-x003","symbol":"\\rho_{k,c}","meaning":"Time period when the shiftable load k for load-shift interval c begins consuming; used to compute the consumption delay in the shifting payment.","kind":"operational","domain":"period index determined from the END-OFF binary by Eq. (16); the source does not state an explicit numerical domain beyond the shiftable interval context","unit":"period number","indices":["k \\in K^{SP}","c \\in C(k)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev27","v141-b-g02-ev31","v141-b-g04-e06"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-x004","symbol":"\\chi_{g,t}^{Gr}","meaning":"Total amount of electricity generation curtailed for the reducible generator unit g during period t; multiplies the reducible-generator contract curtailment price in the payment/cost term.","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative active energy curtailed [kWh], bounded by forecasted generation in Eq. (2) for g in G^r","unit":"kWh","indices":["g \\in G^{r}","t \\in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev10","v141-b-g02-ev11","v141-b-g04-e06"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-x005","symbol":"\\chi_{g,t}^{Gd}","meaning":"Total amount of electricity generation curtailed for the disconnectable generator unit g during period t; multiplies the disconnectable-generator contract curtailment price in the payment/cost term.","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative active energy curtailed [kWh], equal to \\delta^{G}_{g,t} F^{G}_{g,t} in Eq. (3) for g in G^d","unit":"kWh","indices":["g \\in G^{d}","t \\in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev10","v141-b-g02-ev11","v141-b-g04-e06"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-theta001","symbol":"P_k^{CD}","meaning":"Contract disconnection fee for load unit k in K^{CD}; the source describes it as the price for disconnecting load k during a period, while the printed symbol P_k^{CD} omits a t index.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"NOK","indices":["k \\in K^{CD}"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev24","v141-b-g02-ev02","v141-b-g04-e02"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-theta002","symbol":"P_k^{SP}","meaning":"Contract price for shifting load unit k in K^{SP} one period; the source calls it the cost per time unit settled in the flexibility contract.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"NOK/period","indices":["k \\in K^{SP}"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev32","v141-b-g02-ev02","v141-b-g04-e02"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-theta003","symbol":"V_{k,c}^{start}","meaning":"Start-period of forecasted consumption of load unit k during shift time interval c; the base-case beginning of the energy profile.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"period number","indices":["k \\in K^{SP}","c \\in C(k)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev26","v141-b-g02-ev32","v141-b-g04-e05"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-theta004","symbol":"P_{g,t}^{Gr}","meaning":"Contract price in the local flexibility market for curtailing the reducible generator unit g in G^r during period t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"NOK/kWh","indices":["g \\in G^{r}","t \\in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev12","v141-b-g02-ev02","v141-b-g04-e02"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-theta005","symbol":"P_{g,t}^{Gd}","meaning":"Contract price in the local flexibility market for curtailing the disconnectable generator unit g in G^d during period t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"NOK/kWh","indices":["g \\in G^{d}","t \\in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev12","v141-b-g02-ev02","v141-b-g04-e02"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The SESP market subsystem manages local flexibility transactions, including settlement, billing and accounting applications. Scope: Settlement administration within the SESP market subsystem for local flexibility transactions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-015"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Flexibility revenues are paid according to the flexibility contracts under the pay-as-contract arrangement. Scope: Flexibility-provider revenues in the SESP-operated local flexibility market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-008"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Participants with activated resources are subsequently rewarded according to their flexibility contracts. Scope: Rewards to participants whose resources are activated in response to DSO requirements. Condition: The participant's resources have been activated.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-010"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The flexibility cost used to determine compensation for curtailable and shiftable loads does not depend on the amount of activated energy. Scope: Compensation for flexibility supplied by curtailable and shiftable loads. Condition: Flexibility from a curtailable or shiftable load is activated.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev03"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The disconnection cost equals the number of disconnected periods multiplied by the load's disconnection fee. Scope: Contractual flexibility charges for curtailable disconnectable loads. Condition: A curtailable disconnectable load is disconnected.","expression":"P_k^{CD} \\sum_{t \\in T} (\\delta_{k,t}^{start}+\\delta_{k,t}^{run}), \\quad \\forall k \\in K^{CD}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-x001","v141-c-R006-x002"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R006-theta001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev24","v141-b-g02-ev01","v141-b-g02-ev02"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C006","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The shifting cost equals the consumption delay multiplied by the cost per time unit established in the load's flexibility contract. Scope: Contractual flexibility charges for shiftable profile loads. Condition: A shiftable load's consumption is delayed relative to its baseline start.","expression":"P_k^{SP} (\\rho_{k,c}-V_{k,c}^{start}), \\quad \\forall k \\in K^{SP},\\ c \\in C(k)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-x003"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R006-theta002","v141-c-R006-theta003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev32","v141-b-g02-ev31","v141-b-g02-ev01","v141-b-g02-ev02"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C007","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Generator-curtailment fees are established in the agreed flexibility contract, with prices specified period by period for reducing or disconnecting generation. Scope: Contractual flexibility charges for reducible and disconnectable generators. Condition: Generation is reduced or disconnected.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev12"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C008","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The generator-curtailment payment component in the SESP cost objective is the period-by-period contract price for reducing or disconnecting generation multiplied by the corresponding curtailed energy, summed over reducible and disconnectable generators and periods.","expression":"\\sum_{t \\in T} \\left( \\sum_{g \\in G^{r}} P_{g,t}^{Gr} \\chi_{g,t}^{Gr} + \\sum_{g \\in G^{d}} P_{g,t}^{Gd} \\chi_{g,t}^{Gd} \\right)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-x004","v141-c-R006-x005"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R006-theta004","v141-c-R006-theta005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-ev01","v141-b-g02-ev02","v141-b-g02-ev12"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-001","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"be In order to run these markets, local traders need the SESP Platform for or sending information, t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A local flexibility market (LFM) is an electricity trading platform to sell and buy flexibility in geographically limited areas like neighbourhoods and small towns. The SESP is the local market platform provider and community aggregator (AGR). At the same time, the SESP is a BRP from the regulatory point of view because it bids in wholesale markets. In order to run these markets, local traders need the SESP Platform for sending information, trading for flexibility, and scheduling actions."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-008","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"deﬁned by the SESP. Low price ﬂexible assets will be activated more often than high price ones. Addi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to avoid market dominance and over-costs, the flexibility revenues are paid-as-contract. As flexibility contracts can be updated periodically, daily and weekly modifications could be found. Due to the lack of experience from prosumers creating bids, the LFM is organized in pay-as-contract, a similar way like the so called pay-as-bid. The pay-as-clear approach would increase the cost of flexibility for the DSO because all providers would receive the clearing price, and for all society at the end."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-010","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"re e- i- ty ed he Fig. 3. Consumer’s ﬂexibility oﬀers example. ed y- resources sorted from the cheap","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Therefore, according to the DSO requirements to manage power quality issues, the SESP decides which resources are necessary to meet the request and sends the control signals to them. After that, the participants with activated resources are then rewarded based on their flexibility contract."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-015","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The domains aﬀected cover from prosumers and DER installations D up to the distribution grid. The zo","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The zones identified as Market and Enterprise comprise three subsystems that make SESP operation possible. They are the market, control and metering systems. The market is responsible for the management of transactions needed to implement the local flexibility market. It covers energy scheduling, flexibility, settlement, billing and accounting applications. The control subsystem is in charge of the management of the orders determined in the market. The metering subsystem manages the data resulting from smart meters (SM) and local controllers (LC) on the field zone."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev03","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"886","section":"4.1. Objective function","anchor_text":"ed 20 Notice that the cost for using ﬂexibility from curtailable and shif- al table loads is not dep","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Notice that the cost for using flexibility from curtailable and shiftable loads is not dependent of the energy activated. This approach avoids disputes after the operation day, to determine the economic compensation for the activated flexibility."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev12","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":"887","section":"4.2. Flexible generator model","anchor_text":"P. Olivella-Rosell et al. (δgG,t ) to deﬁne if the generator g is disconnected or not during period ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The cost of curtailing a generator is a fee established in the agreed ﬂexibility contract. Particularly, it is deﬁned the price of reducing or disconnecting energy generation, period by period, and is represented by PgGr,t and PgGd,t respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev24","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":"888","section":"4.4.1. Curtailable disconnectable load model","anchor_text":"P. Olivella-Rosell et al. t + Dkmax ∑ δkend,i ⩾ δkstart,t ∀ k ∈ K CD ,∀ t ∈ T po i = t (13) The cost","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The cost of disconnecting load k  is the number of periods dis-connected times its disconnection fee (PkCD)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev32","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p08-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":"888","section":"4.4.2. Shiftable profile load model","anchor_text":", nd Tkend,c − (V kend,c − Vkstart,c ) me ρk ,c = ∑ γk ,t · t ∀ k ∈ K SP ,∀ c ∈ C (k ) t = Tkstart,c","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The cost for shifting the load k is deﬁned by the consumption delay ( ρk ,c −Vkstart,c  ) times the cost per time unit (PkSP) settled in its ﬂexibility contract."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev01","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"886","section":"4.1. Objective function","anchor_text":"ed 20 Notice that the cost for using ﬂexibility from curtailable and shif- al table loads is not dep","equation_id":"Eq. (1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"min f_{obj}^{LFM} = \\sum_{t \\in T} \\Big( \\sum_{g \\in G^{r}} P_{g,t}^{Gr} \\chi_{g,t}^{Gr} + \\sum_{g \\in G^{d}} P_{g,t}^{Gd} \\chi_{g,t}^{Gd} + \\sum_{b \\in B} \\big( P_{b,t}^{B,in} \\sigma_{b,t}^{in} + P_{b,t}^{B,out} \\sigma_{b,t}^{out} \\big) + \\sum_{k \\in K^{CD}} P_k^{CD} \\cdot (\\delta_{k,t}^{start} + \\delta_{k,t}^{run}) \\Big) + \\sum_{k \\in K^{SP}} \\sum_{c \\in C} P_k^{SP} \\cdot (\\rho_{k,c} - V_{k,c}^{start}) \\quad (1)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev02","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p06-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":"886","section":"4.1. Objective function","anchor_text":"ng PgGr,t χ· gGr,t : cost of reducing generation output of the unit g ∈ Gr during • ty period t PgGd","equation_id":"Eq. (1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"• P_{g,t}^{Gr}χ_{g,t}^{Gr}: cost of reducing generation output of the unit g ∈ G^{r} during period t\n• P_{g,t}^{Gd}χ_{g,t}^{Gd}: cost of disconnecting the generator g ∈ G^{d} during period t\n• P_{b,t}^{B,in}·σ_{b,t}^{in}, P_{b,t}^{B,out}·σ_{b,t}^{out}: cost of charging or discharging the battery unit b during period t, respectively\n• P_k^{CD}·(δ_{k,t}^{start}+δ_{k,t}^{run}): cost of switching off the curtailable disconnectable load k ∈ K^{CD} during period t\n• P_k^{SP}·(ρ_{k,c}−V_{k,c}^{start}): cost of shifting ρ_{k,c}−V_{k,c}^{start} periods the shiftable load k ∈ K^{SP} during shifting period c"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev10","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p06-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"886","section":"4.2. Flexible generator model","anchor_text":"of he 4.2. Flexible generator model m- on Flexible generation installations with remote control capa","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Flexible generation installations with remote control capability can provide downward regulation during periods of energy surplus. There are two types of curtailable generators: reducible ( g ∈ Gr) and dis-connectable ( g ∈ Gd). Reducible generators can receive control signals of energy production adjusting their power output during a speciﬁc period of time. In contrast, disconnectable generators are those that can only be switched on and oﬀand they cannot receive setpoints.\nThe decision variables for reducible and disconnectable production are χgGr,t and χgGd,t respectively and they represent the amount of active energy curtailed."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev11","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":"887","section":"4.2. Flexible generator model","anchor_text":"P. Olivella-Rosell et al. (δgG,t ) to deﬁne if the generator g is disconnected or not during period ","equation_id":"Eq. (2), Eq. (3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"0 ⩽ χ gGr,t ⩽ F gG,t  ∀ g ∈ G r ,∀ t ∈ T                                   (2)\n\n0 ⩽ χ gGd,t = δgG,t · F gG,t  ∀ g ∈ G d ,∀ t ∈ T                               (3)\n\nwhere χgGr,t and χgGd,t represent the ﬂexibility activated and their setpoints\nare the diﬀerence between the forecasted production and the ﬂexibility\nrequested."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev18","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":"887","section":"4.4.1. Curtailable disconnectable load model","anchor_text":"Fig. 6. Comparison of two ﬂexible loads type behaviour under the same command sig- nals. s- applies ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Curtailable disconnectable loads (KCD) are those ﬂexible loads that do not consume the curtailed energy once they are reconnected. CD loads can be for example programmable space heaters with a scheduled consumption. If the reconnection signal arrives out of the time program, the control signal will not switch the load on.\nThey are remotely controlled with binary signals OFF (δkstart,t  ) and END-OFF (δkend,t  ). When an OFF order (δkstart,t = 1) is sent to the curtailable load k, independently of the baseline status, the load is switched oﬀ.\nWhen the load receives an END-OFF order (δkend,t = 1 ), the load goes back to the baseline consumption proﬁle. Additionally, the time between the OFF and END-OFF signals is calculated using the binary variable δkrun,t  .\nFor example, if the OFF signal is 1 during period t = 2 (δkstart,2 = 1) and the END-OFF signal is 1 during period t = 8 (δkend,8 = 1), then δkrun,t  is 1 between t ∈ [3,7]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev26","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":"888","section":"4.4.2. Shiftable profile load model","anchor_text":"p gy p p , washing machines, dryers, electric water heaters, heat pumps, and electric vehicle charge","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Flexibility contract deﬁnes the shiftable period c for each appliance k with the parameters Tkstart,c  and Tkend,c which determine the time span in which is possible to schedule consumption. Within this shiftable period c, the forecasted consumption  is denoted with Vkstart,c  and Vkend,c  re-presenting the beginning and ending of the energy proﬁle in the base case."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev27","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":"888","section":"4.4.2. Shiftable profile load model","anchor_text":"p k c, k c, p en which is possible to schedule consumption. Within this shiftable period start end l","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Additionally, γk t, is the binary variable which indicates the END-OFF signal. For example, γk t, ∗ = 1 if ρk c, = t ∗ being ∗t the period to send the END-OFF signal."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev31","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p08-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":"888","section":"4.4.2. Shiftable profile load model","anchor_text":", nd Tkend,c − (V kend,c − Vkstart,c ) me ρk ,c = ∑ γk ,t · t ∀ k ∈ K SP ,∀ c ∈ C (k ) t = Tkstart,c","equation_id":"Eq. (16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Once the new proﬁle is established, Eq. (16) deﬁnes the starting period (ρk c, ) to calculate the corresponding ﬂexibility cost of load k in shifting period c in the objective function. The cost for shifting the load k is deﬁned by the consumption delay ( ρk ,c −Vkstart,c  ) times the cost per time unit (PkSP) settled in its ﬂexibility contract.\nTkend,c − (V kend,c − Vkstart,c  )\nρk ,c =  ∑      γk ,t · t  ∀ k ∈ K SP ,∀ c ∈ C (k )\n                                        t = Tkstart,c                                                 (16)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-e02","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p13-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":13,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"P. Olivella-Rosell et al. Table A.4 Contract price parameters. PgGr,t Price in local ﬂexibility gene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table A.4","image_ref":"pages/page-13.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Table A.4\nContract price parameters.\nP^{Gr}_{g,t} Price in local flexibility market contract for curtailing the reducible generator unit g ∈ G^{r} during period t [NOK/kW h]\nP^{Gd}_{g,t} Price in local flexibility market contract for curtailing the disconnectable generator unit g ∈ G^{d} during period t [NOK/kW h]\nP^{B,in}_{b,t} Price to charge the battery unit b during period t [NOK/kW h]\nP^{B,out}_{b,t} Price in local flexibility market contract for discharging the battery unit b during period t [NOK/kW h]\nP^{CD}_{k} Price in local flexibility market contract for disconnecting the load unit k ∈ K^{CD} during period t [NOK]\nP^{SP}_{k} Price in local flexibility market contract for shifting the load unit k ∈ K^{SP} one period [NOK]"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p13-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":13,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"the load unit k [ Dkmax Maximum curtai [# of periods] Vkstart,c Start-period of fo during shift time","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table A.7","image_ref":"pages/page-13.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Table A.7\nFlexible load parameters.\nW^{CD}_{k,t} Curtailable load consumption forecast for the load unit k during period t [kW h]\nW^{SP}_{k,t} Shiftable load consumption forecast for the load unit k during period t [kW h]\nN^{max}_{k} Maximum number of disconnections for the load unit k during the planning horizon T [#]\nD^{min}_{k} Minimum time duration between two curtailments of the load unit k [# of periods]\nD^{max}_{k} Maximum curtailment duration of the load unit k [# of periods]\nV^{start}_{k,c} Start-period of forecasted consumption of the load unit k during shift time interval c [#]\nV^{end}_{k,c} End-period of forecasted consumption of the load unit k during shift time interval c [#]\nT^{start}_{k,c} Earliest possible start period for shifting the load unit k during time interval c [#]\nT^{end}_{k,c} Latest possible end period for shifting the load unit k during time interval c [#]"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p14-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":14,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"P. Olivella-Rosell et al. Table A.8 Variables χgGr,t Total amount of electr the generator unit g d χ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table A.8","image_ref":"pages/page-14.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Table A.8\nVariables\nχ^{Gr}_{g,t} Total amount of electricity generation curtailed of reducible the generator unit g during period t [kW h]\nχ^{Gd}_{g,t} Total amount of electricity generation curtailed of disconnectable the generator unit g during period t [kW h]\nδ^{G}_{g,t} Binary variable = 1 if curtailment of the disconnectable generator unit g is applied during period t, else 0\nσ^{in}_{b,t} Energy charged by the storage unit b during period t [kW h]\nσ^{out}_{b,t} Energy discharged by the storage unit b during period t [kW h]\nσ^{soc}_{b,t} State of charge of the storage unit b during period t [kW h]\nδ^{out}_{b,t} Binary variable = 1 if the battery unit b is discharging electricity during period t, else 0\nδ^{start}_{k,t} Binary variable = 1 if curtailment of the disconnectable load unit k starts during period t, else 0\nδ^{run}_{k,t} Binary variable = 1 if curtailment of the disconnectable load unit k is running in time period t, else 0\nδ^{end}_{k,t} Binary variable = 1 if curtailment of the disconnectable load unit k ends during period t, else 0\nω_{k,t} Delivered energy to the shiftable load unit k during period t [kW h]\nγ_{k,t} Binary variable = 1 if the shiftable load k begins consuming at period t, else 0\nρ_{k,c} Time period when the shiftable load k for load shift interval c begins consuming [#]"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-activation","v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-001","quote":"The SESP is the local market platform provider and community aggregator (AGR)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-015","quote":"The market is responsible for the management of transactions needed to implement the local flexibility market. It covers energy scheduling, flexibility, settlement, billing and accounting applications."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-008","quote":"In order to avoid market dominance and over-costs, the flexibility revenues are paid-as-contract."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-010","quote":"After that, the participants with activated resources are then rewarded based on their flexibility contract."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev03","quote":"Notice that the cost for using flexibility from curtailable and shiftable loads is not dependent of the energy activated. This approach avoids disputes after the operation day, to determine the economic compensation for the activated flexibility."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev24","quote":"The cost of disconnecting load k  is the number of periods dis-connected times its disconnection fee (PkCD)."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev32","quote":"The cost for shifting the load k is deﬁned by the consumption delay ( ρk ,c −Vkstart,c  ) times the cost per time unit (PkSP) settled in its ﬂexibility contract."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev12","quote":"The cost of curtailing a generator is a fee established in the agreed ﬂexibility contract. Particularly, it is deﬁned the price of reducing or disconnecting energy generation, period by period"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"0de8ead1a949870efe49cf4ca4ebf8bb85ef739c7951939e87bb98b1986227e1","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The source supplies explicit contract-price payment/cost expressions for CD-load disconnection, SP-load shifting, and generator curtailment (Eq. (1), its cost definitions, and Tables A.4/A.8). The remaining administrative pay-as-contract and settlement-scope statements lack an explicit algebraic formula in the supplied source and remain procedural. B evidence is unreviewed; this formalization does not assert independent source verification.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001"],"rationale":"C001 is the procedural statement linked by the frozen edge from the SESP/local operator to the settlement.payment node."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-x001","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The start-of-disconnection binary determines the period count entering the CD-load settlement payment term; it is a payment determinant bound to settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-x002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The running-disconnection binary determines the period count entering the CD-load settlement payment term; it is a payment determinant bound to settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-x003","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The shift start period rho determines the consumption delay used in the SP-load payment term; it is bound to settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-x004","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Curtailed reducible-generator energy is the quantity multiplied by the contract curtailment price in the generator payment term."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-x005","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Curtailed disconnectable-generator energy is the quantity multiplied by the contract curtailment price in the generator payment term."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-theta001","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The CD-load disconnection fee is a contract parameter used to compute the disconnection payment; bound to settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-theta002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The SP-load per-period contract price is a contract parameter used to compute the shifting payment; bound to settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-theta003","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The baseline start-period of a shiftable load enters the delay expression used in the shifting payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-theta004","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The reducible-generator contract curtailment price is a payment/cost parameter for generator curtailment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-theta005","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The disconnectable-generator contract curtailment price is a payment/cost parameter for generator curtailment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C005","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The formalized CD-load disconnection cost term expresses settlement.payment for curtailable disconnectable loads; no frozen edge directly encodes the arithmetic."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C006","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The formalized SP-load shifting cost term expresses settlement.payment for shiftable-profile loads; no frozen edge directly encodes the arithmetic."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C008","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The formalized generator-curtailment cost term is an additional explicit payment component for reducible and disconnectable generators under settlement.payment."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
